WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.235
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.904
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.972
[ Cheers and applause ]
Welcome!

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:09.108
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.377
Thank you for watching.
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:12.878
Well, guys, this is big.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.914
Last night,
"Time" magazine announced

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:19.352
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris
as 2020's Person of the Year.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.254
Yeah.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.256
After the announcement,
Trump called Rudy Giuliani

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.757
and was like,
"Forget the election.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.360
We're suing 'Time' magazine."

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.195
Apparently,
"Time" magazine was like,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.563
"There's so many worthy people,

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.666
but who would annoy Trump
the most?"

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.135
I got to be honest,

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.436
I thought it was going to be
frontline healthcare workers,

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:38.871
especially since
doctor's offices

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.741
is the only place you still find
a copy of "Time" magazine.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.710
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.378
That's right.

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:48.481
They picked Biden and Harris
over Trump.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.982
Even worse, the original cover

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:52.752
was the two of them
going down a ramp.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.220 line:0%
That's -- Oh.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.955 line:0%
"I had very slippery shoes on.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:59.058
And I couldn't do it.
It was very slippery."

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:01.494
That's right. Trump and his
staff were pretty annoyed

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.763
that he wasn't named
"Time's" Person of the Year,

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.566
but they managed grabbed a
couple of other magazine covers.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.033
Let me show you what I mean.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.435
Trump was honored by a magazine

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:12.272
which covers two of his
favorite things, food and whine.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.707
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:19.179
Michael Flynn received the honor
from "Better Homes &amp; Pardons."

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:23.082
Steve Mnuchin
was honored by "Mnewsweek."

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:25.051
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.690
Wilbur Ross was featured
on the cover of...

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.559
"One Hundred Seventeen."

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.393
That's...

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.695
Mike Pence was given the honor
from something called

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:38.231
"This is a Magazine."

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.833
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.334
And, finally, Rudy Giuliani

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.336
was featured in
"Field &amp; Streaming."

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.704
Yeah, there you go, everybody.
Congrats.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.740
Congrats to you guys
on those covers.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.108
And this is just wild.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:51.777
It just came out
that Trump's chief of staff

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.979
told the head of the FDA
to approve

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:57.784
the Pfizer vaccine today
or resign.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.453
Trump's like,
"We need this vaccine today

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.922
for a virus
I've ignored since March.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.457
We need it today!"

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.525
[ Applause ]

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.360
I think we let the FDA
have their moment.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.698
I mean, 80% of their job is just
putting out lettuce recalls.

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:15.768
Give them a little something.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.169
I got to say, though,
in Trump's defense,

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:20.439
if the FDA is allowing
Pizza Hut's triple-decker box,

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:22.575
then this should not
be a problem.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.743
Meanwhile, I saw that Walmart

00:02:24.743 --> 00:02:27.880
is preparing to administer
COVID vaccines at its stores.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.149
[ Applause ]
That's the good news.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.884
The bad news is they're
gonna be given to you

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:33.953
by a Walmart greeter.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:37.022
"Hold still.

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:39.859
Oh, here comes
the pointy airplane.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.728
Oh, I'm going down.
I'm going down.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.829
Come down with me.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:46.065
There's no way I'm getting up.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.367
You've got to come down here
to get the shot."

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.537
Reminds me of a few years ago
when my uncle

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:53.506
had a heart valve replaced
at K-Mart.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.475
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:59.044
Actually, Walmart's
a great place to give vaccines

00:02:59.044 --> 00:03:02.182
'cause no one's
wearing sleeves anyway.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.317
Here's some big
entertainment news.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.953
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.355
Here's some big
entertainment news.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.857
Disney just held
their annual Investor Day

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:14.059
